---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE, formatSiteAddress } from '../config/site';

const telHref = `tel:${(SITE.phoneDisplay ?? SITE.phone).replace(/\D/g, '')}`;
const address = formatSiteAddress();
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE.name}`}
  description={SITE.policyDescription}
>
  <Header />
  <main class="section legal-page">
    <div class="container legal-content panel-card">
      <p class="section-label">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: July 22, 2026</p>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>{SITE.name}</strong> (“we,” “us,” or “our”) collects,
        uses, and shares information when you visit our website, request service, schedule
        an appointment, or otherwise contact us. The practices described here reflect how a
        {SITE.city} / {SITE.region} {SITE.serviceNoun} company typically handles customer data.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>We may collect information you provide directly, including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Name, phone number, email address, and property address</li>
        <li>Service details and project notes</li>
        <li>Preferred appointment windows and messages you send through forms or chat</li>
        <li>Photos or documents you voluntarily upload related to a job</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may also collect limited technical information automatically, such as:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Browser type, device type, approximate location derived from IP address</li>
        <li>Pages visited, referral source, and general site-usage metrics</li>
        <li>Cookies or similar technologies used for basic analytics and site performance</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
      <p>We use collected information to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Respond to service, estimate, and appointment requests</li>
        <li>Schedule appointments, coordinate crews, and communicate project updates</li>
        <li>Provide quotes, warranties, and post-project follow-up</li>
        <li>Improve our website, services, and local service coverage</li>
        <li>Send marketing messages only when you have opted in</li>
        <li>Comply with legal obligations and protect against fraud or misuse</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. SMS &amp; Phone Communications</h2>
      <p>
        If you provide a phone number and consent to be contacted, we may call or text you about your
        estimate, consultation, or project status. Message frequency varies.
        Message and data rates may apply. Reply <strong>STOP</strong> to opt out of SMS at any time;
        reply <strong>HELP</strong> for help. SMS consent is not a condition of purchase and is not
        sold or shared with third parties for their own marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>4. How We Share Information</h2>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information. We may share information with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Service providers who help us operate forms, hosting, analytics, or communications</li>
        <li>Financing partners, only when you request financing options</li>
        <li>Insurance carriers or adjusters, only when you ask us to support a claim</li>
        <li>Professional advisors or authorities when required by law or to protect our rights</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Any vendors we use are expected to process information only as needed to perform services for
        us and to protect it with reasonable safeguards.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Cookies &amp; Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Our site may use cookies or similar tools to remember preferences, measure traffic, and
        understand how visitors find our services. You can control cookies through your browser
        settings. Disabling cookies may affect some site features.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep estimate and project-related information for as long as needed to provide services,
        maintain warranty records, resolve disputes, and meet legal or accounting requirements. When
        information is no longer needed, we delete or de-identify it when reasonably practical.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your Choices &amp; Rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Request access to personal information we hold about you</li>
        <li>Ask us to correct inaccurate information</li>
        <li>Request deletion of information, subject to legal or warranty retention needs</li>
        <li>Opt out of marketing emails or texts</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To make a request, contact us using the details below. We may need to verify your identity
        before fulfilling certain requests.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Children’s Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our services are intended for adults seeking residential and commercial {SITE.serviceNoun} work. We do
        not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child
        has submitted information, contact us and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Data Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards to protect information
        submitted through our site. No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure, so we cannot
        guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Third-Party Links</h2>
      <p>
        Our website may link to Google Maps, financing partners, or other third-party sites. Their
        privacy practices are governed by their own policies, not this one.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top will
        change when we do. Continued use of the site after updates means you acknowledge the revised
        policy.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this Privacy Policy or your information:
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>{SITE.name}</strong><br />
        {address}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a><br />
        Phone: <a href={telHref}>{SITE.phone}</a><br />
        License: {SITE.license}
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding-top: 5.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 4rem;
    background: var(--panel);
  }

  .legal-content {
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .legal-content h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--deep);
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal-content h2 {
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.55rem;
    color: var(--deep);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .legal-content p,
  .legal-content li {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-content ul {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .legal-content a {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
